"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"past participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having gored"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வெண்ணார்","parts":[{"text":"வெண்ணார்","lemma":"வெண்ணார்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கொண்டு","parts":[{"text":"கொண்டு","lemma":"கொண்டு","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கைசுவைத்","parts":[{"text":"கைசுவைத்","lemma":"கைசுவைத்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தண்ணாந்","parts":[{"text":"தண்ணாந்","lemma":"தண்ணாந்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"தழுங்க","parts":[{"text":"தழுங்க","lemma":"தழுங்க","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"னெஞ்சமொடு","parts":[{"text":"னெஞ்சமொடு","lemma":"னெஞ்சமொடு","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"முழங்கும்","parts":[{"text":"முழங்கும்","lemma":"முழங்கும்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"அத்தம்","parts":[{"text":"அத்தம்","lemma":"attam","gloss":"desert path"}],"gloss":"desert path"},{"surface":"நீள்","parts":[{"text":"நீள்","lemma":"nīḷ","gloss":"long"}],"gloss":"long"},{"surface":"இடை","parts":[{"text":"இடை","lemma":"iṭai","gloss":"way/distance"}],"gloss":"distance"},{"surface":"அழ","parts":[{"text":"அழ","lemma":"aḻa","gloss":"to weep"}],"gloss":"to weep"},{"surface":"பிரிந்தோர்","parts":[{"text":"பிரி","lemma":"piri","gloss":"part/separate"},{"text":"ந்து","lemma":"ntu","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ōr","gloss":"pronominal suffix"}],"gloss":"those who parted"},{"surface":"ஏ","parts":[{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis particle"}],"gloss":"indeed"}]}],"literal":"Like a broken bangle, for many to worship, / in the red-mouthed sky, beautifully appearing, / yet again is born the crescent moon, alas! / Did he forget, indeed, he himself? The male elephant, its / languishing-paced gentle female elephant's suffering unable to bear, / so that the tall-standing Yā tree is ruined, goring, / taking the white bark fiber, chewing with its trunk, looking up with open mouth, / with a distressed heart, roaring, / in the long distance of the desert path, leaving me to weep, he who parted.","translation":"Alas! The crescent moon, looking like a broken bangle, has appeared beautifully in the red-hued evening sky for many to worship. Did he forget me? He who parted from me, leaving me to weep, and went through the long desert path where the male elephant, unable to bear the suffering of its languishing, gentle mate, gores the tall Yā tree to ruin, takes its white bark fiber, chews it with its trunk, and then, looking up with open mouth, roars with a distressed heart.","modern":"உடைந்த வளையலைப் போலப் பலரும் தொழும்படி, செவ்வானத்தில் அழகாகத் தோன்றி, மீண்டும் பிறை நிலவு பிறந்துவிட்டது, அந்தோ! மெல்ல நடக்கும் தன் பெண் யானையின் பசியைத் தாங்க முடியாமல், ஆண் யானையானது உயரமான யா மரத்தை வேரோடு அழியும்படி குத்தி, அதன் வெண்மையான நாரை எடுத்துத் தன் துதிக்கையால் சுவைத்து, பின் அண்ணாந்து பார்த்து வருத்தத்தோடு பிளிறும் நீண்ட பாலைவன வழியில், என்னை அழவிட்டுப் பிரிந்து சென்றவர், என்னை மறந்துவிட்டாரோ?","explanation":"The heroine is speaking to herself or her friend in the evening, expressing her deep grief during the separation from her lover. She sees the new crescent moon rising in the evening sky, which reminds her of her loneliness and the passage of time. She wonders if her lover, who went away to earn wealth through the harsh desert path, has forgotten her. The poem belongs to the pālai (desert) landscape, symbolizing separation. The image of the male elephant goring the Yā tree to feed its suffering mate shows the deep love and empathy in nature, which contrasts with her own lover leaving her to suffer alone.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.2,0.61],[0.61,0.85],[0.85,1.3],[1.3,1.8],[1.8,2.2],[2.2,2.53],[2.53,2.73],[2.8,3.3],[3.3,4.1],[4.1,4.7],[4.7,5.1],[5.1,5.3],[5.3,6.1],[6.1,6.5],[6.5,7.0],[7.0,7.6],[7.6,8.7],[8.7,9.3],[9.33,9